EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Fallen_Fane_Characters_Quirinus" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Fallen Fane - Quirinus"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-09"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Fallen_Fane_Core_Ext"

    # Quirinus (The Characters, p35): one player character, its sheet the DESCRIPTION.

    #t93ef0e91989d670c368d41 ^"Quirinus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"House" STRING "Bonisagus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t5a0fd5af2e6babcd30d36c ^"Durenmar (The Fallen Fane)"]
            ^"Rank" STRING "Archmage"
            ^"Position" STRING "Praeco"
            ^"Character Priority" INTEGER 1
            ^"Printed Introduction" STRING "You are an Archmage, a member of House Bonisagus, a member of Durenmar, and the Praeco."
            ^"Source" STRING "The Fallen Fane"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 35
        }
        DESCRIPTION "You are an Archmage, a member of House Bonisagus, a member of Durenmar, and the Praeco. Read the paragraph about the Praeco’s duties carefully, and fulfill them as honestly as you can. You have quite a bit of leeway without actually cheating.\n\nAquila, a young upstart covenant, has recently been pestering Durenmar to give up one of the rights guaranteed to House Bonisagus by the Code of Hermes, and to allow other covenants access to a village which produces a large number of Gifted individuals, about one every five years. They have threatened to raise it at tribunal, but you don’t think that there is really much of a threat. The right of House Bonisagus to claim apprentices is clear from the Code, after all.\n\nIt is customary for all the Archmages to meet together at the Tribunal, and decide how the various issues should be decided, for the good of the Order as a whole. These meetings normally take place a little time into the Tribunal, to give the Archmages a chance to learn about all the issues that will be raised. The decisions of this meeting are not binding, but the Archmages can use their votes (or other powers) and influence to ensure that the whole Tribunal agrees.\n\nViridia, the maga carrying most of Durenmar’s sigils, has told you that she wishes to speak to you, and the other Bonisagi attending the Tribunal, about a matter of great importance to the House and Order. She has emphasised that it is to be kept secret, and also that she does not wish to discuss it only with other members of Durenmar. You are curious, and have agreed to speak to her during the meeting."
    }

}
